# Part B — Implementation Plan

## Scene Architecture

| Scene | Root Node | Key Children | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|-------------|---------|
| Main.tscn | Node2D | GameManager, DayNightCycle, WeatherSystem | Master scene, owns all global state |
| Diner.tscn | Node2D | TileMapLayer, ParallaxBackground, CounterZone, CorkboardZone, SpawnPoints | The only playable space — 2D cross-section |
| Player.tscn | CharacterBody2D | AnimatedSprite2D, CollisionShape2D, InteractionArea (Area2D) | Side-view player controller; Area2D detects nearby interactables |
| NPC.tscn | CharacterBody2D | AnimatedSprite2D, NavigationAgent2D, DialogueTrigger | Shared base scene for all NPCs |
| CounterZone.tscn | Node2D | Area2D, ItemSpawnPositions | Area where NPCs leave items for pickup |
| CookingUI.tscn | CanvasLayer | PantryPanel, VirtualCounter (2D), CombineButton, ResultSlot | 2D overlay; all cooking happens here |
| CorkboardUI.tscn | CanvasLayer | ItemSlots, CloseUpView | Full-screen corkboard examination view |
| UI.tscn | CanvasLayer | RecipeLog, DialogueBox, RelationshipMeter, SavingsDisplay, DayTransition | All HUD and UI panels |

## Scripts

| Script | Attached To | Responsibility |
|--------|-------------|---------------|
| game_manager.gd | Autoload | Global state: day count, weather, NPC roster, player savings, save/load |
| day_night_cycle.gd | DayNightCycle | Phase switching, time advance, overnight recipe trigger, stale item check |
| weather_system.gd | WeatherSystem | Daily fog/rain roll; updates ParallaxBackground tint and NPC spawn conditions |
| player.gd | Player.tscn root | A/D movement, AnimatedSprite2D state machine, Area2D interaction detection (E key) |
| cooking_ui.gd | CookingUI.tscn root | Manages 2D overlay: pantry icons, drag-and-drop to virtual counter, combination lookup, result display |
| combination_db.gd | Autoload | Single Dictionary of all recipes: {sorted_pair} -> result. One source of truth. |
| npc_base.gd | NPC.tscn root | Spawn at entrance, NavigationAgent2D pathfinding to seat, animation state machine, relationship meter, payment on serve |
| npc_data.gd | Autoload | All NPC definitions: affinities, dialogue tiers, schedule conditions, payment amounts, items they leave |
| dialogue_manager.gd | Autoload | Serve correct dialogue tier based on current relationship meter value |
| corkboard_ui.gd | CorkboardUI.tscn root | Track pinned items, display full-screen examination view, trigger NPC dialogue unlocks |
| economy.gd | Autoload | Track player savings, passage cost, payment from NPC serves, ending threshold check |
| recipe_log.gd | UI RecipeLog panel | Display discovered/undiscovered combos; filter views (all, overnight, mystery) |
| diner_progression.gd | Diner.tscn root | Swap diner tile/decoration layers (early/mid/late game) at story milestones |

## Build Stages

### Stage 1 — Project Setup & Player Movement (Week 1)
- Create Godot project, set up folder structure, initialise Git
- Build Player.tscn: CharacterBody2D + AnimatedSprite2D, A/D movement, W/S for ladders
- Block out Diner.tscn with placeholder tiles — walls, floor, counter, windows, door
- Set up ParallaxBackground with placeholder gradient layers
- Set up Camera2D following the player (clamped to diner bounds)
- Confirm player can walk around the diner and see the parallax background through windows

### Stage 2 — Cooking UI & Combination System (Weeks 2–3)
- Build CookingUI.tscn as a CanvasLayer overlay (C key to open/close)
- Pantry panel on left: ingredient icons the player can drag from
- Virtual counter in centre: two slots, player drags ingredients into them
- Implement combination_db.gd with 10 test recipes as a Dictionary
- On combine: look up {ingredient_a, ingredient_b} sorted pair, spawn result icon or show fail state
- Recipe log UI shows discovered combos; undiscovered shown as ???

> ⚠ **Tricky:** drag-and-drop in Godot's Control nodes uses `_get_drag_data` and `_drop_data`. Set this up with a simple test icon before building the full pantry.

### Stage 3 — Day / Night Cycle & Overnight Recipes (Week 3)
- DayNightCycle script: day/night state machine, advance day on player action
- On day advance: fire a `day_advanced` signal that all systems subscribe to
- Swap ParallaxBackground tint and diner lighting (CanvasModulate or PointLight2D) between phases
- Overnight recipe check: if an ingredient flagged 'overnight' has been in the UI counter 1+ nights, transform it to the result
- Stale check: increment counter per item each day; at threshold replace with stale version

### Stage 4 — NPC Pipeline & Economy (Weeks 4–5)
- Build NPC.tscn: CharacterBody2D with AnimatedSprite2D, NavigationAgent2D pathfinding to a seat
- Animations: idle, walk, sit, eat, react, leave (sprite sheet frames)
- One NPC spawns at night at the diner door, walks to seat, waits, reacts to served dish, pays player, leaves
- Relationship meter increases/decreases based on dish served
- Dialogue triggers at tier thresholds (3 tiers minimum for test NPC)
- economy.gd tracks savings; SavingsDisplay UI shows current total and passage cost
- NPC leaves a sprite item at the CounterZone on arrival or departure; player picks it up with E (Area2D overlap)

> ⚠ **Tricky:** NavigationRegion2D baking. Bake as soon as diner tilemap is blocked out. Re-bake whenever tile layout changes.

### Stage 5 — Corkboard (Week 5)
- CorkboardUI.tscn: full-screen CanvasLayer with item slot positions
- Player picks up corkboard item from counter (same E-to-pickup as ingredients)
- Pin to corkboard: item appears in the corkboard UI at the next free slot
- R key near corkboard opens the full-screen UI; player can examine item text/illustration

### Stage 6 — Content Build (Weeks 6–11)
- All NPC arcs scripted (deep arcs first, then medium, then light)
- 120+ combinations loaded into combination_db.gd from the design spreadsheet
- All 2D environment tiles and sprite assets created as pixel art
- All NPC sprites with full animation sets
- All 2D ingredient and dish icons created and integrated into CookingUI
- Parallax backgrounds for all weather/time-of-day states
- Environmental progression: 3 visual tile/decoration swaps at story milestones
- Full audio pass: ambient tracks, SFX, weather transitions

### Stage 7 — Both Endings (Weeks 11–12)
- economy.gd ending threshold check: when savings >= passage cost, offer the choice
- Ending A (Leave): player confirms payment, departure sequence and ending screen
- Ending B (Stay): player declines, final scene mirrors Traveller arc opening
- Baker arc finale: Pressed Flower chain completes, Memory Cake unlocks full ending dialogue
- Soft fail recovery: overnight offering mechanic for departed NPCs

### Stage 8 — Polish & Export (Weeks 13–14)
- Full playthrough of both endings; fix any blocking bugs
- Balance pass: payment amounts, passage cost, relationship meter decay rates
- Main menu, settings screen, save/load (day count, savings, relationships, recipes, corkboard)

## Potential Problems & How to Avoid Them

| Problem | When | How to avoid it |
|---------|------|-----------------|
| Drag-and-drop in Control nodes | Stage 2 | Test with a single draggable icon before building the full pantry. Use `_get_drag_data` / `_drop_data`, not mouse events. |
| NavigationRegion2D baking | Stage 4 | Bake nav region as soon as diner tilemap exists. Re-bake on any tile layout change. Don't leave it until Stage 6. |
| Combination dict growing large | Stage 6 | Keep combination_db.gd as a single Autoload. All 120+ recipes in one Dictionary. Never split across files. |
| Overnight timing bugs | Stage 3 | Use one `day_advanced` signal. All overnight/stale checks subscribe to it. No duplicate timers anywhere. |
| Economy balance | Stage 7 | Design passage cost and NPC payment amounts in a spreadsheet first. Tune values in one place (game_manager or economy.gd constants). |
| Sprite animation management | Stage 4–6 | Use a consistent sprite sheet format (e.g. 64×64 per frame, 8 frames per row). Standardise frame counts early. |
| TileMap complexity | Stage 1 | Start with a single TileMapLayer for collision geometry, add decoration layers later. Don't try to tile everything at once. |
| Scope overrun | Ongoing | Protect both endings above all else. If behind: cut light-arc NPCs to 4, reduce combos to 90, defer audio polish. |
